| Las Vegas | +1.23 |
| Houston | +1.01 |
| Austin | +0.78 |
| ... | ... |
| Dallas | −0.50 |
| New York | −0.69 |

**11 positive, 7 negative, mean ~+0.18.** Before the trimmed mean it was +0.7 to
+1.1 in 17 of 18 cities. **The one-directional bias is gone. Consensus is
calibrated.** The clock is closed.

Watch Vegas (+1.23) and Houston (+1.01) — still meaningfully cold.

**SIGN CONVENTION — read before interpreting any bias number.**
`errors = actual − consensus`. A POSITIVE value means settlement came in WARMER
than predicted, i.e. **the model runs COLD**. Misreading this caused a wrong
call on Aug 24.

