## 📋 MANUAL RESEARCH — SCHEDULE, now evidence-backed

**Log the TOP BRACKET only, at three passes:**

| Pass | Band | Basis |
|---|---|---|
| **10:30–11:00 AM ET** | 60–69¢ | +16.93 / +10.80 |
| **12:00 PM ET** | 60–69¢ | +12.18 |
| **4:00 PM ET** | 70–79¢ (60–69 also OK) | +6.36 / +4.38 |

### The finding that matters: the BAND, not the minute

60–69¢ was positive at **10 of 11 hours** and at **all twelve 15-minute slices**
tested between 10am and 1pm:

10:00 +4.62 · 10:15 +9.09 · 10:30 **+16.93** · 10:45 +14.19 · 11:00 +10.80 ·
11:15 +7.53 · 11:30 +12.89 · 11:45 +13.85 · 12:00 +12.18 · 12:15 +9.05 ·
12:30 +6.59 · 12:45 +6.67

**The ordering is noise.** 10:00 is the worst cell and 10:30 the best, thirty
minutes apart. Cells are ~80 correlated observations. An earlier read that "noon
beats 12:45 because of the cost-of-certainty curve" did NOT survive — the same
four-point decline inside the noon hour does not appear inside the 10am or 11am
hours. Average across all twelve is ~+10¢. **Pick a time that fits the day.**

### The CEILING does the work, not the floor

Open-ended floors are all bad because they drag in the 80+ tier, which wins
85–96% and pays nothing at 87–94¢:

| floor | negative at |
|---|---|
| 50c+ | 7 of 11 hours |
| 55c+ | 6 of 11 hours |
| 60c+ | 7 of 11 hours |

The **band** 60–69 was positive at 10 of 11. **Screen 60–69, not "60 and over."**

### 55–59 does not hold up

Across 9:00–11:30 ET: +6.89, +2.91, −1.02, −0.14, +8.27, +0.84. Three near zero,
one negative, flips sign. Average ~+2.9 against 60–69's ~+8.3. **Skip it.**
(Logging those rows anyway to build your own sample is defensible — costs a line.)

### The afternoon trend — the most convincing pattern found

| ET | 60–69 | 70–79 | 70–79 win% |
|---|---|---|---|
| 2pm | −0.42 | −6.99 | 66.7% |
| 3pm | +0.50 | +3.88 | 78.2% |
| 4pm | +4.38 | +6.36 | 80.6% |
| 5pm | +7.17 | **+10.41** | 84.6% |

**Win rate climbs 66.7% → 84.6% while the price stays flat near 74¢.** That is
the market failing to reprice as certainty increases — a cleaner structural
signal than anything in the morning cells. 5pm is best; 4pm gives up ~4¢ for a
workable hour; 3pm is where it gets thin.

### Per-city (12:45 ET, 60c+, before the ceiling was established)

Positive: San Antonio +25.47, Austin +22.79, LAX +18.38, OKC +17.43, Vegas
+14.56, Phoenix +6.70, Dallas +5.13, Miami +3.13, NY +0.76, Philadelphia +0.50.
Negative: Houston −11.14, Atlanta −11.40, Chicago −17.00, DC −23.11.

Ten of fifteen positive. Winners skew south/west, losers north/east. **n=5–17 per
city — nowhere near the discipline bar.** Do not build an allowlist on this yet.

